<BaseLayout title="About"><div class="shell"><header class="page-heading"><h1>About me</h1></header>
<div class="prose"><p>I am Zinuo (Henry) You, a PhD researcher in Engineering Mathematics and Computer Science at the University of Bristol. I work at the intersection of generative modelling, reinforcement learning, and optimization.</p>
<p>My research spans long-horizon video and world models, corrective transport, continuous-time generative models, and efficient inference. I work across mathematical formulation, PyTorch implementation, multi-GPU experiments, and evaluation.</p>
<p>Earlier projects explore graph representation learning, black-box Bayesian optimization, and evidence-constrained LLM agents.</p>
<h2>Education</h2><ul><li><strong>University of Bristol</strong> · PhD in Engineering Mathematics and Computer Science, 2023–present.</li><li><strong>University of Sheffield</strong> · MSc in Electronic and Electrical Engineering, Distinction, 2019–2020.</li><li><strong>Southwest University</strong> · Bachelor’s in Electronic Science and Technology / Solid-State Physics, 2015–2019.</li></ul>
<p><a href={site.cvPath}>Download my CV</a> · <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p></div><Experience/></div></BaseLayout>
